[candidate · 2:31] Honestly, I think I can skip ahead here — the answer's pretty clearly input costs. Coffee commodity prices and dairy have spiked over the last two years, and wages in food service have gone up a lot too. Revenue grew 15% but margin fell 18 points, which is exactly what you'd see if COGS and labor inflated and prices stayed flat.

So my recommendation: Brew & Bean should raise menu prices. Specialty coffee is a low-elasticity category — people buy their latte regardless. I'd do a staged increase, maybe 7-10% on core drinks, lead with the premium SKUs where willingness to pay is highest, and pair it with a loyalty program so regulars feel cushioned. That alone should recover most of the margin.

Secondary lever would be renegotiating bean contracts and locking in longer-term supplier pricing to stop the bleeding on volatility.

That's where I'd land.
